# Backtick names with `\` or quotes get a quoted name that lexes back to the same name.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | project `a\b`, `it's "x"`
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..35
  PIPELINE@0..34
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    PROJECT_OP@9..16
      IDENT@9..16 "project"
    WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
    ERROR@17..34
      ERROR@17..22 "`a\\b`"
      COMMA@22..23 ","
      WHITESPACE@23..24 " "
      ERROR@24..34 "`it's \"x\"`"
  WHITESPACE@34..35 "\n"

error[DS0001]: names are not quoted with backticks
  --> query:1:18
  |
1 | from t | project `a\b`, `it's "x"`
  |                  ^^^^^ backticks are not a quote
  |
  = help: quote the name with brackets: `['a\\b']`

error[DS0001]: names are not quoted with backticks
  --> query:1:25
  |
1 | from t | project `a\b`, `it's "x"`
  |                         ^^^^^^^^^^ backticks are not a quote
  |
  = help: quote the name with brackets: `['it\'s "x"']`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from t | project ['a\\b'], ['it\'s "x"']
which parses without errors
